# OpenMFE

> OpenMFE is an open standard for building portable, retrofittable microfrontends with browser-native technology, strong encapsulation, and a formal, machine-readable interface contract (a YAML manifest modelled on OpenAPI).

A microfrontend is a self-contained custom element plus a small backend (BFF) that serves its data, a mandatory prerender endpoint, and an optional semantic (JSON-LD) endpoint. The manifest declares the component's attributes (input) and events (output) as a versioned contract that both human teams and coding agents can build and integrate against.

## Specification
- [OpenMFE specification](https://github.com/openmfe/specification/blob/main/specification.md): the normative rules a compliant microfrontend must follow.
- [Manifest JSON Schema](https://github.com/openmfe/manifest/blob/main/lib/schema.json): the schema the manifest is validated against.

## Build a microfrontend
- [seed repository](https://github.com/openmfe/seed): a minimal working example plus an AGENTS.md that guides a coding agent through building a compliant microfrontend.
- [Devtools](https://openmfe.org/development/openmfe-devtools/): the manifest validator, the contract-history checker, and the runtime checker used to verify a microfrontend against its contract.

